# Replying and reacting, from this end.
#
# Both were decode-only. The transcript could draw a tapback that this client had no way to
# send, and the action bar had said "A reply" since the thread screen was written while the
# press it named built a message that answered nothing.
#
# A aims at the bubble under the cursor and the compose sheet says so with a badge; X puts an
# emoji on the same bubble; Y is still "write", and still answers nothing. The reply that lands
# carries a quote line - a bar and one elided line of what it is answering - inside its bubble.

scene demo
tab messages

# Into the direct conversation with Bravo Creek.
key down 4
key a
hold 600

message in BRVO Found the crossing, about 200m upstream
hold 900

# A: the canned list, aimed at that message. The badge in the app bar is what says so.
key a
hold 1400
key b
hold 500

# X: the tapback picker, on the same bubble.
key x
hold 1200
key down 2
hold 1100
key b
hold 600

# The reply as it lands. There is no app behind the harness, so the send is stood in for.
reply out BRVO On my way
hold 1600

# And a tapback from the other end, drawn as a chip on the bubble it names rather than as a
# bubble holding one glyph.
react BRVO 👍
hold 1800
